README – Calendar Assistant Project

Sonia Yahi  
Allison Arcand

1. Overview
The Calendar Assistant is a full‑stack scheduling application that supports:
Custom login (email + password)
Google OAuth2 login
Event creation
Task creation
Gemini AI chat assistant
React frontend
Node.js/Express backend
MySQL database
This ZIP contains all files needed to understand, run, and reproduce the project.

2-GitHub Repository : 
https://github.com/arcandaatwit/CalendarAssistant.git
2. Folder Structure:

/vsCode
	settings.json
/backend
    Node.js + Express server
    Authentication, Google API integration, Gemini API, CRUD routes

/database
    MySQL schema file

/public
   calicon.png

/src
    App.jsx
    index.jsx
    main.jsx
    index.css
    login.jsx
    profile.jsx
    taskPage.jsx
    addEvent.jsx
    ChatWidget.jsx
    /scheduler
        (scheduler-related components)


3. How to Run the Project
Backend
Go to /backend
Install dependencies:
npm install
Create a .env file containing:
Google OAuth credentials
Gemini API key
MySQL connection info
JWT secret
Start the server:
npm run dev 
Frontend
Go to the root folder (where /src is)
Install dependencies:
npm install
Start the React app:
npm run dev
4. Requirements
Node.js
MySQL
Google Cloud credentials
Gemini API key
